# Sunday 09:30 UTC — weekly, and deliberately nowhere near the digest.
#
# **Weekly rather than daily, and off the digest path, are both still deliberate after the
# move to the metered key.** The daily 05:00 pipeline (ingest -> AI match -> send) is what
# real subscribers are waiting on; an enrichment added to that window does not make a digest
# late, it makes it *miss*, silently, for everyone. This job has no such deadline: the
# residue shrinks a week later instead of a day later and nobody is waiting on it. 09:30 also
# clears the 08:00 source watchdog, the 08:30 categorisation watchdog and the 09:00 digest
# watchdog, so it contends with none of them for RAM or for Postgres.
#
# Steady state is ~2 400 genuinely new titles a week's worth of ingests; the one-off backlog
# on cutover was ~15 100 distinct titles, which the default CATEGORIZE_LIMIT (8 000) drains
# over the first couple of runs, commonest-titles-first. At Haiku 4.5 rates that whole
# backlog is well under a dollar — cost is not what sets this cadence.
[Unit]
Description=JobDigest title classification, weekly on Sunday at 09:30

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Sun *-*-* 09:30:00
Persistent=true
Unit=jobdigest-categorize.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
